The Windows interruption path now applies the same five-second cleanup bound to
both `taskkill` and the post-termination child wait instead of allowing either
operation to block indefinitely. Focused lifecycle regressions cover a hung
`taskkill`, a child that survives `taskkill`, and the normal interrupted Windows
process-tree cleanup, while the full packaging suite remains green.

A current full Windows x64 Shipping run then published `dist/windows-x64`
through the canonical runner. The unpruned publication contained 30 files and
